<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $000038AE)
【拓巳】
“W-Well, I think I’m used to it by now, sorta...”
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $000038F0)
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $000039AC)
PK stands for “player kill.”
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $000039BC)
In other words, it’s when you go around in MMOs killing randos%N
and stealing their gold and gear. So, typical DQN stuff.
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $000039F4)
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00003ABC)
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00003B84)
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00003C40)
...Well, except for the rules that prohibited RMT. I broke%N
those all the time. Fuhihi.
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00003CDE)
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00003D9A)
New Gen? What was that?%NHad he ever mentioned it before?
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00003DAA)
Grimm was talking like I should’ve already known about it.
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00003DCA)
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00003F0E)
Oh, now that he’d mentioned it, I *did* feel like I’d heard%N
about it somewhere...
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00003F1E)
Though, all I knew was that they existed.%N
I hadn’t looked into them at all.
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00003F9A)
I tried googling “New Gen” and instantly got a few results.
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00004006)
【拓巳】
“Let’s see here...”
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00004016)
【拓巳】
“Looks like ‘New Gen’ is the name for two incidents in%N
 Shibuya that happened in the past month...”
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00004026)
【拓巳】
“Including a fetus, there’ve been seven victims.”
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $0000408C)
【拓巳】
“The first incident was the Group Dive, where five friends%N
 jumped off a skyscraper...”
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $0000409C)
【拓巳】
“And in the second one, a fetus was found inside a man’s body...”
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $000040AC)
【拓巳】
“Whoa, are you serious...?”
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $000040CE)
A chill ran down my spine.
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $0000417A)
Before I’d even realized it, I’d turned around and was looking%N
around my room again.
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $0000422E)
There were a bunch of results for “New Gen” on Taboo! News, so%N
I went to skim through them.
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $0000423E)
New Generation Madness—the incidents that had the entire%N
Internet in an uproar.
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $0000424E)
There’d been two of them so far.
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $0000425E)
One of them was so brutal, several TV channels didn’t even%N
describe the crime out loud.
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $0000426E)
The first incident, the Group Dive, had been initially%N
thought to be a suicide, but rumors had since risen%N
that it may not’ve been.
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $0000427E)
Parents and friends of the five victims all said the%N
same thing—none of the victims had shown any signs of%N
planning to commit suicide, and they hadn’t had any%N
reason to do so, either.
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $0000428E)
And on top of that, some physical evidence had been found too.
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $000042EA)
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $000043F4)
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00004508)
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $000045E6)
【拓巳】
“He’s getting a kick out of this...”
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $000045F6)
He did stuff like this from time to time.
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00004606)
But if I wanted to keep up my reputation as the great Neidhardt of%N
Baselard, I couldn’t let it faze me.
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00004616)
Unlike in the real world, I was a god in the world of ESO.%N
I was the strongest, wisest, and most noble knight in all the land.%N
Mocking me would be a fool’s errand.
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00004626)
And so, gathering up whatever courage I had, I clicked the link.
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $000046A0)
Oh, it was just some shitty doodle.
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $000046E4)
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $000047AC)
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $000048D0)
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $000049D2)
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00004B20)
Come to think of it, that Shogun guy had been here the whole time.%N
I’d completely forgotten about him. Not that I cared, though.
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00004B30)
Well, I don’t really feel like sleeping yet, so I guess I’ll farm%N
in ESO for a bit.%N
...Wait, no, the new episode of Blood Tune comes out today!
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00004B40)
I didn’t have a TV in my room, so I just made do with my PC.
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00004B50)
【拓巳】
“Fifteen minutes to go...%N
 Might as well go to the bathroom while I wait.”
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00004B60)
I took a quick look at Seira next to my monitor.%N
I would get to see Seira-tan today... I couldn’t wait!
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00004B70)
With that on my mind, I made my way over to close the chat window...
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00004BA6)
【拓巳】
“Huh?”
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00004BB6)
Shogun had sent a message.
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00004BC6)
【拓巳】
“Wh-What the? He actually posted...”
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00004BD6)
So he wasn’t just a lurker? 
<LINE>
Judging by the file extension, it looked like an image link.
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00004BE6)
A sudden link, posted by a suspicious stranger that hadn’t sent a%N
single message until now. I gulped instinctively.
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00004BF6)
I couldn’t explain why, but I had a bad feeling about it—a feeling%N
unlike anything I had ever felt in all my time on the Internet.%N
I really didn’t want to click it.
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00004C06)
I clicked my tongue and glanced at the clock. My rendezvous with%N
Seira-tan was in twelve minutes. I should probably get this%N
conversation over with quickly.
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00004C3E)
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00004D28)
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00004DE4)
I was trying my best to act calm and casual.
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00004DF4)
To be honest, I really didn’t want to chat with%Na shady guy like this.%N
I was so uncomfortable that I could feel a cold sweat forming.
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00004E04)
And if the guy only spoke German,%N
I definitely wouldn’t be able to deal with him.
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00004E3A)
Huh, so he could actually speak normally...
<LINE>
I relaxed a little bit.
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00004E5A)
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00004F2A)
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $0000501C)
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $000050D8)
For some reason, there was a short pause.
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $000052EE)
【拓巳】
“...”
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $000052FE)
All at once, images of those gruesome New Gen incidents flashed%N
through my head.
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $0000530E)
Even though I hadn’t actually seen any photos, I could picture them
 so vividly that it was almost like I’d been there myself.
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $0000531E)
The man’s torn-up stomach... The lifeless fetus shoved inside...%K
<LINE>
The five people that dove off the building, instantly turning%N
into a pulpy inhuman puddle upon hitting the ground...
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $0000532E)
Just thinking about it was almost enough to make me puke.%K
<LINE>
I shook my head violently, as if to shake the gruesome delusion%N
out of my head.
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $0000533E)
This Shogun guy was so suspicious, I couldn’t stop the paranoid%N
delusions from forming.%K What was he trying to drag me into?
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $0000535E)
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00005426)
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00005510)
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $000055F6)
【拓巳】
“What’s that?”
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00005606)
Was this Shogun guy some kind of **denpa** nutjob?
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00005616)
I’d never seen that formula before in my life.%N
And when you were as smart as me, that was saying something.
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00005676)
I tried looking it up.
<LINE>
In this day and age, there was all sorts of information on the%N
Internet, so it’d be easy to find.
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00005686)
【拓巳】
“...Huh. I’m not getting any results.”
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00005696)
Was he trying to act smart by typing some nonsense formula?
<LINE>
Fuck if I knew.
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $000056EA)
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $000057B2)
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $0000587A)
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00005C44)
【拓巳】
“...”
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00005C54)
All of a sudden, the chat was flooded with links.
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00005C64)
Just who was this guy...?%N
Was he just trying to scare me for shits and giggles?%N
Maybe he was a friend of Grimm’s,%N
and they’d teamed up to mess with me.
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00005D2C)
【拓巳】
“...”
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00005D92)
Feeling the “gaze” again, I took a look around the room.
<LINE>
But surprise, surprise, all that was behind me was darkness and%N
clutter, as per usual.
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00005DA2)
I was hit with an unnatural sense of dread.%N
The feeling of perpetually being watched left me feeling restless.
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00005E08)
【拓巳】
“Don’t... look at me.”
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00005E18)
And upon saying that, I realized that my voice was trembling.
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00005E28)
It was almost like the cluttered room I knew so well had%N
transformed into someplace completely foreign.
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00005E38)
If you’ve ever had to go to the bathroom at night after watching a%N
horror movie or listening to a ghost story or something,
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00005E48)
you may know the feeling of being unnerved, or even terrified,%N
by the dark hallways of your own home.
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00005E58)
That was close to how I felt right now.
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00005F20)
【拓巳】
“D-Dammit, you think this shitty bait’s gonna faze me...?”
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00005F30)
In spite of my shuddering, I faced the monitor, leaned in, and...
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00005F40)
...before I knew it, with the slightest twitch of my index finger,%N
I’d clicked one of the links.
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $00005F5C)
【拓巳】
“No, wai—!”
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $0000606A)
I really had no clue how it’d happened. It wasn’t like my hand had%N
been possessed by some unnatural force or something...%N
I’d just sort of... done it without thinking.
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $0000607A)
But even though I knew full well that it’d be a mistake,%N
I’d clicked it as if it were the most natural thing in the world.
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $0000608A)
【拓巳】
“Ugh, what is this...?”
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $0000609A)
The image that filled my monitor...
<LINE>
looked like some kind of modern art piece.
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $000060AA)
An arrangement of spikes, like the quills of a hedgehog or pins in%N
a pin cushion, protruded from the wall in the shape of a cross.%N
Below it, a puddle of dark red.
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $000060BA)
And in front of it... were small pieces of something, scattered%N
across the ground like garbage.
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $000060CA)
Seriously, what even was this?
<LINE>
The work of some pretentious “avant-garde” artist?
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $000060DA)
Those sorts of idiots were all over the place. They’d make gory%N
stuff like this, then spout some bullshit like,%N
“It depicts the latent chaos oft laid bare in this cruel world!”
<LINE>
No way in hell I’d ever consider that shit “art”...
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $000060EA)
Still, what a weird image.
<LINE>
It hadn’t explicitly been gore, but it was definitely borderline.
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $000060FA)
So then, why...
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $0000610A)
Why had it seemed so graphic?
<LINE>
Why had it seemed so realistic?
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $0000611A)
Why was I imagining the stench of blood?%N
And why was that stench so strong that it nearly made me choke?
<LINE>
It was all in my head, so why did I feel sick to my stomach?
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $0000612A)
I felt a sharp, throbbing pain in my forehead.
<LINE>
The nausea wouldn’t go away.
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $0000613A)
【拓巳】
“Guh, ghhh...”
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $0000614A)
I desperately reached for my mouse, but my trembling hand knocked%N
it off the desk, leaving it dangling above the floor by its cord.%N
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $0000615A)
I reeled it back up to the mousepad, and then,%N
finally, closed the image.
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $000061D6)
But... just as I thought it was finally over,%N
my eyes were struck by...
<END>

#WRITE(PTR, $000061E6)
